  "live_records": {
    "q-112200": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112200",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $|8-2x|=5,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|8-2x|=8-2x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|8-2x| & =5 \\\\ 8-2x & =5 \\\\ -2x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & =\\frac{-3}{-2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|8-2x|=-(8-2x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|8-2x| & =5 \\\\ -(8-2x) & =5 \\\\ -8+2x & =5 \\\\ 2x & =13 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{13}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
